cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Laminar: Infrastructure for laminar stacking (default: honeycomb symmetry, JAM notation)"
abstract: >
  Laminar is a Rust workspace for the exact enumeration, canonicalization,
  classification, and export of stacking configurations in honeycomb
  layered materials. The default (and only) instantiation in v0.1 targets
  honeycomb layers with JAM notation; the architecture supports additional
  symmetry modules and notations via the StackingMode trait. Ships with a
  CLI and Python bindings.
